.el .ds Aq '
.TH garuda-toolbox-packages-search 1  "garuda-toolbox 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
garuda\-toolbox\-packages\-search \- Search the repository and installed packages by name and description, or the AUR with `\-\-aur`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgaruda\-toolbox packages search\fR [\fB\-\-installed\fR] [\fB\-\-orphans\fR] [\fB\-\-aur\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR \fIWHEN\fR] [\fB\-\-width\fR \fICOLUMNS\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fITEXT\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Search the repository and installed packages by name and description, or the AUR with `\-\-aur`
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-installed\fR
Only the installed packages
.TP
\fB\-\-orphans\fR
Only the dependencies no installed package needs any more
.TP
\fB\-\-aur\fR
Search the AUR instead, also its keywords, the exact name first. Downloads the AUR\*(Aqs package list when the last try is a day old. Works while the window\*(Aqs AUR setting is off: the flag asks for it
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON instead of text, for scripts
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print the programs\*(Aq own words under an error
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Print long text directly instead of through `$PAGER`
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Colour the output: auto, always or never
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-width\fR \fI<COLUMNS>\fR
Cut long cells to this many columns
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Leave out the spinner and the hints
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fITEXT\fR]
Only the packages whose name or description contains this text, in any case. Without it every package
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  garuda\-toolbox packages search editor
  garuda\-toolbox packages list \-\-installed
  garuda\-toolbox packages search \-\-orphans \-\-json
  garuda\-toolbox packages search \-\-aur paru
.SH ALIASES
\fBgaruda\-toolbox packages list\fR
.SH "SEE ALSO"
garuda\-toolbox\-packages(1), garuda\-toolbox(1)
